.TH geectl-remote-download 1  "geectl-remote-download 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-download \- Download a source file to a local path. The binary counterpart of `cat`: the library streams the file to disk instead of reading it as a UTF\-8 string, so a binary file (a source tarball) downloads instead of failing the UTF\-8 check, and a file larger than the transport\*(Aqs 10 MiB body cap downloads instead of failing. A read: `\-\-live` is ignored, like `cat`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote download\fR [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-output\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download a source file to a local path. The binary counterpart of `cat`: the library streams the file to disk instead of reading it as a UTF\-8 string, so a binary file (a source tarball) downloads instead of failing the UTF\-8 check, and a file larger than the transport\*(Aqs 10 MiB body cap downloads instead of failing. A read: `\-\-live` is ignored, like `cat`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
Download the file as of this revision: a revision number or a srcmd5 (default: latest)
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Where to write the downloaded bytes
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package the file lives in
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The file to download
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
